Object.assign(window.EXAMPLES=window.EXAMPLES||{},{"mabini":{"t":"Apolinario Mabini’s life","c":"Apolinario Mabini was a Filipino lawyer and political thinker, known as the ‘Brains of the Revolution’. Though paralysed from the waist down by illness in 1896, he became Emilio Aguinaldo’s chief adviser, drafting decrees and a constitution for the revolutionary government, and served as its first prime minister. Captured by the Americans, he was exiled to Guam for refusing to swear allegiance to the United States. He died of cholera soon after returning in 1903.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 288\" width=\"640\" height=\"288\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"272\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1864</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Tanauan, Batangas</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1896</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Paralysed by illness</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1898</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Becomes Aguinaldo’s chief adviser</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1899</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">First prime minister of the republic</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1901</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Exiled to Guam</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"244\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1903</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Returns and dies of cholera</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Mabini’s life"}]},"aluna":{"t":"Antonio Luna’s life","c":"Antonio Luna was a Filipino scientist, journalist and general during the Philippine–American War. Trained as a pharmacist and chemist in Europe, where he joined the Propaganda Movement, he founded the newspaper La Independencia and set up a military academy. Known for his brilliance and fierce temper, he tried to impose strict discipline on the army, which made him enemies. He was killed by soldiers of the revolutionary army in Cabanatuan in June 1899. His brother was the painter Juan Luna.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1866</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1890s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Studies science in Europe</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1898</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Founds La Independencia</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1899</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Leads Filipino forces against the Americans</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">5 Jun 1899</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Killed in Cabanatuan</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Luna’s life"}]},"silang":{"t":"Gabriela Silang’s revolt","c":"Gabriela Silang was an Ilocana leader who continued the revolt against Spanish rule begun by her husband, Diego Silang, in the Ilocos region. After Diego was assassinated in 1763, she led the rebel forces for about four months, attacking the town of Vigan, before being captured and executed. She is remembered as one of the first women to lead a revolt in the Philippines, and the women’s organisation GABRIELA is named after her.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1731</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Ilocos</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1762</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Diego Silang leads a revolt in Ilocos</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">May 1763</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Diego is assassinated</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1763</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Gabriela leads the revolt</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sep 1763</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Captured and executed</text></svg>","c":"A revolt in Ilocos, 1762–63"}]},"jesus":{"t":"The life of Jesus","c":"Jesus of Nazareth was a Jewish preacher and teacher in Roman-ruled Judea and Galilee in the 1st century, and the central figure of Christianity, whose followers believe he is the Son of God and the Messiah. Most of what is known about him comes from the four Gospels of the New Testament. He taught love of God and neighbour, often through parables, and was crucified in Jerusalem on the orders of the Roman governor Pontius Pilate. Christians believe he rose from the dead. In Islam, he is honoured as a prophet, Isa.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">c.4 BC</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Bethlehem, according to the Gospels</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Grows up</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">In Nazareth, Galilee</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">c.AD 28–30</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Teaches and heals around Galilee</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">c.AD 30–33</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crucified in Jerusalem</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Today</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">About 2.4 billion people are Christians</text></svg>","c":"His life as told in the Gospels (dates approximate)"}]},"muhammad":{"t":"The life of the Prophet Muhammad","c":"Muhammad was born in Mecca, in Arabia, around 570. Muslims believe he was the final prophet of God, to whom the Qur’an was revealed through the angel Gabriel over 23 years. Facing persecution in Mecca, he and his followers moved to Medina in 622, the Hijra, which marks the start of the Islamic calendar. By his death in 632, most of Arabia had accepted Islam. Out of respect, Muslims traditionally do not depict him in pictures, and say ‘peace be upon him’ after his name.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 288\" width=\"640\" height=\"288\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"272\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">c.570</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Mecca</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">610</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">First revelation, in a cave near Mecca</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">622</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The Hijra: migration to Medina</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">630</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Returns to Mecca</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">632</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies in Medina</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"244\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Today</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">About 2 billion people are Muslims</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in his life"}]},"hokusai":{"t":"Katsushika Hokusai’s life","c":"Katsushika Hokusai was a Japanese artist and printmaker of the Edo period, and one of the most famous artists in the world. He produced around 30,000 works, including paintings, book illustrations and woodblock prints. His series ‘Thirty-six Views of Mount Fuji’, around 1831, includes ‘The Great Wave off Kanagawa’, one of the best-known images ever made. He used about 30 different names during his career and kept working into his late eighties. His art influenced European painters such as Monet and Van Gogh.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1760</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Edo (now Tokyo)</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1779</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Publishes his first prints</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1814</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">First volume of his sketchbooks, the Hokusai Manga</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">c.1831</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Thirty-six Views of Mount Fuji</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1849</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies, aged 88</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Hokusai’s life"}]},"documentary":{"t":"Kinds of documentary film","c":"A documentary is a non-fiction film that records real life, people and events, to inform, persuade or preserve a record. Early examples include ‘Nanook of the North’ (1922). Lightweight cameras in the 1960s let filmmakers follow events as they happened, and streaming has made documentaries more popular than ever. Even documentaries involve choices about what to film, include and leave out, so viewers are encouraged to think about the filmmaker’s point of view.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Expository</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">A narrator explains a topic</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Observational</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The camera quietly follows events</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Participatory</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The filmmaker takes part and interviews</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Poetic</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Images and mood more than facts</text></svg>","c":"Four common styles"}]},"inequality":{"t":"Measuring inequality","c":"Poverty means lacking enough money to meet basic needs such as food, clean water, shelter, health care and education. Extreme poverty has fallen dramatically since 1990, but hundreds of millions of people, many in sub-Saharan Africa, still live on less than about three US dollars a day. Inequality is about how unevenly income and wealth are shared. Economists often show it with a Lorenz curve: the further the curve sags below the line of perfect equality, the more unequal the society, measured by the Gini coefficient from 0 (equal) to 1. Simplified.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 290\" width=\"600\" height=\"290\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:580px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M80,250L380,30\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><path d=\"M80,250C200,240 300,200 380,30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M80,250L380,30C300,200 200,240 80,250Z\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".15\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"276\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Share of people, poorest to richest →</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 56 140)\">Share of income →</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#16a34a\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Perfect equality</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Real country</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Shaded gap = inequality</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Bigger gap, higher</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Gini coefficient</text></svg>","c":"A Lorenz curve (simplified)"}]},"overtourism":{"t":"Overtourism and responses","c":"Overtourism happens when so many visitors come to a place that it harms the environment, the quality of life of residents or the visitor experience itself. Popular cities, islands and natural sites from Venice and Barcelona to Kyoto and Bali have seen protests by residents. Places have responded with entry fees, visitor limits, bans on new hotels or holiday rentals and campaigns to spread tourists out. Since 2024, for example, Venice has charged day-trippers on busy days.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 232\" width=\"610\" height=\"232\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crowds</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Packed streets and sites</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#f97316\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rising rents</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Homes turned into holiday rentals</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Damage</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Litter, erosion and stressed wildlife</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Entry fees and caps</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Limit numbers at busy times</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"158\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Spread visitors out</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Promote off-season and lesser-known places</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"158\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rules for rentals</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Limit short-term lets</text></svg>","c":"Problems (top) and common responses"}]},"volunteering":{"t":"Ways to volunteer","c":"Volunteering means giving time and effort to help others or a cause, without being paid. Volunteers run food banks, coach sports, care for the environment, teach, help in hospitals, respond to disasters and more. The United Nations estimates that hundreds of millions of people volunteer each year, much of it informally, by helping neighbours. Volunteering benefits communities and can improve volunteers’ own wellbeing, skills and friendships. International Volunteer Day is 5 December.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 232\" width=\"610\" height=\"232\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Community</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Food banks, clean-ups, helping neighbours</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Education</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Tutoring and mentoring</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Health and care</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Hospitals and elderly care</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#f97316\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Disaster relief</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rescue, shelter and supplies</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"158\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#15803d\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#15803d\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Environment</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Tree planting and wildlife</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"158\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Online</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Translating, mapping and research</text></svg>","c":"Six ways people help"}]},"automation":{"t":"Which work is easiest to automate?","c":"Automation means using machines and computer systems to do work that people once did. It began with factory machines and has spread to robots, self-service checkouts and software. Artificial intelligence is now automating some office and creative tasks. Automation can raise productivity and remove dangerous or dull work, but can also eliminate jobs, so retraining and education are important. History suggests new kinds of jobs also appear, though not always for the same people.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Easier to automate</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Repetitive, predictable, rule-based tasks</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f97316\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#f97316\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Examples</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Data entry, assembly lines, routine checks</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Harder to automate</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Care, creativity and judgement</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Examples</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Nursing, plumbing, teaching, research</text></svg>","c":"Tasks, not whole jobs, are usually automated"}]},"ubi":{"t":"The four features of universal basic income","c":"Universal basic income is the idea that governments should give every adult a regular cash payment, whether or not they work, enough to cover basic needs. Supporters say it would reduce poverty, simplify welfare and give security as automation changes work. Critics say it would be very expensive, could discourage work and would give money to people who do not need it. Trials have taken place in Finland, Kenya, the United States and elsewhere, with mixed and debated results.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Universal</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Paid to everyone</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Unconditional</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">No need to work or look for work</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Regular</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Paid at set intervals, such as monthly</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Cash</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Spent however people choose</text></svg>","c":"What makes it different from other welfare"}]},"onlinelearning":{"t":"Ways of learning online","c":"Online learning means studying through the internet, from full degree programmes to short videos and language apps. During the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020, schools in most countries closed, and over a billion students switched to learning from home, revealing big gaps in access to devices and internet. Online learning offers flexibility and reaches people far from schools, but many learners find it harder to stay motivated and miss face-to-face contact.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Live classes</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Everyone joins at the same time</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Self-paced courses</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Watch and work when you like</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">MOOCs</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Free or cheap courses for thousands</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blended learning</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Part online, part in class</text></svg>","c":"Four common formats"}]},"mentalyouth":{"t":"Young people and mental health","c":"Adolescence is a time of big changes, and many mental health conditions begin then: the World Health Organization says half of all mental health conditions start by age 14, though most cases go undetected and untreated. Stress at school, bullying, family problems, poverty and, for some, heavy social media use can affect young people’s wellbeing. Sleep, exercise, friendships, trusted adults and early support all help protect mental health.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Half by 14</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Half of conditions start by age 14 (WHO)</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Common struggles</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Anxiety, depression and stress</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">What helps</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sleep, exercise, friends, time offline</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Ask for help</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Talk to a parent, teacher or counsellor</text></svg>","c":"Mental health in the teenage years"}]},"memes":{"t":"The life cycle of a meme","c":"An internet meme is an idea, joke, image, video or phrase that spreads rapidly online, usually changing as people copy and remix it. The word ‘meme’ was coined by biologist Richard Dawkins in 1976 for any idea that spreads from person to person. Memes can be silly, clever or political, and brands and campaigns now use them. Because they spread so quickly, memes can also carry misinformation.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1. Created</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">An image, clip or phrase is posted</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2. Shared</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">It spreads across apps and sites</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3. Remixed</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">People add their own versions</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#64748b\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">4. Fades</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">It becomes old news, or a classic</text></svg>","c":"How a meme spreads and fades"}]},"esports":{"t":"Popular kinds of esports","c":"Esports are organised, competitive video gaming, often between professional teams, watched by millions online and in packed arenas. Top tournaments offer prize money in the millions of dollars. Esports are especially popular in South Korea and China, and have spread worldwide. They were a medal event at the 2022 Asian Games, held in 2023, and the International Olympic Committee has run its own esports events. Concerns include long training hours and player wellbeing.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 232\" width=\"610\" height=\"232\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Battle arenas (MOBAs)</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Two teams of five destroy each other’s base</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Shooters</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Teams compete in first-person combat</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Battle royale</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Last player or team standing wins</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Fighting games</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">One-on-one duels</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"158\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sports games</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Football, basketball and racing</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"158\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0891b2\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#0891b2\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Strategy</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Build, plan and outthink opponents</text></svg>","c":"Six common types"}]},"kdrama":{"t":"What makes a Korean drama","c":"Korean dramas, or K-dramas, are television series from South Korea, part of the ‘Korean Wave’ (Hallyu) of popular culture that also includes K-pop and films. They are known for tightly plotted stories, often in a single season of around 16 episodes, mixing romance, comedy, family drama, history, fantasy and thrillers. Streaming services have made them hugely popular across Asia and the world; ‘Squid Game’ (2021) became one of Netflix’s most-watched series ever.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">One season</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Often about 16 episodes, with an ending</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#db2777\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Many genres</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Romance, history, fantasy, thrillers</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Soundtracks</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Songs by popular singers</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Global fans</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Subtitled in dozens of languages</text></svg>","c":"Common features"}]},"shortvideo":{"t":"Vertical versus horizontal video","c":"Short-video apps let people watch and create clips usually lasting from a few seconds to a few minutes, filmed vertically to fill a phone screen. Viewers swipe from one video to the next, while algorithms learn what each person watches and serve more of it. The format has created new trends, music hits and careers. Concerns include how much time people spend on them, effects on attention and young people’s wellbeing, misinformation and data privacy. Simplified.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 330\" width=\"620\" height=\"330\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:560px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"60\" y=\"25\" width=\"140\" height=\"250\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#1e293b\"/><rect x=\"68\" y=\"33\" width=\"124\" height=\"234\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c4b5fd\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Vertical (9:16)</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"318\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Short-video apps</text><rect x=\"280\" y=\"70\" width=\"280\" height=\"160\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#1e293b\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"78\" width=\"264\" height=\"144\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#bfdbfe\"/><text x=\"420\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Horizontal (16:9)</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"318\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">TV, films, older videos</text><path d=\"M130,130l-14,-20h28z\" fill=\"#5b21b6\"/><path d=\"M130,170l-14,20h28z\" fill=\"#5b21b6\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#3b0764\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Swipe</text></svg>","c":"Short-video apps fill the phone screen upright (simplified)"}]},"superhero":{"t":"Superheroes through the decades","c":"Superheroes are fictional characters with extraordinary powers or abilities who fight evil, usually with a secret identity and a distinctive costume. They began in American comic books in the late 1930s and spread into television, cartoons, games and films. Heroes have also come from Japan, with masked heroes and giant robots, and from many other countries’ comics. Since the 2000s, superhero films have become some of the highest-earning movies in history.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1938</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The first costumed superhero comic books (USA)</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1940s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Golden Age of comics; heroes in wartime</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1960s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Heroes with flaws and everyday problems</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1966</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Japanese TV heroes and giant robots appear</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2000s–</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Superhero films become global hits</text></svg>","c":"How the genre grew"}]},"cosplay":{"t":"What goes into cosplay","c":"Cosplay, short for ‘costume play’, is dressing up as a character from anime, manga, comics, films, games or books, often with homemade costumes, wigs, make-up and props. The term was coined in 1984 by Japanese writer Nobuyuki Takahashi after visiting a science fiction convention in the United States. Cosplayers gather at fan conventions, take part in contests and share photos online. Many see it as a creative art form and a way to make friends.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#db2777\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Costume</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sewn, bought or adapted</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Props</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Made from foam, plastic or 3D printing</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Wigs and make-up</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">To match the character</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Performance</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Poses and acting in character</text></svg>","c":"Four parts of a cosplay"}]},"phbio":{"t":"Some of the Philippines’ unique wildlife","c":"The Philippines is one of the world’s 17 ‘megadiverse’ countries, home to a huge share of Earth’s plant and animal species. Because its more than 7,600 islands were isolated for so long, many species live nowhere else, especially mammals, birds, reptiles and plants. It is also a biodiversity hotspot, meaning much of this life is threatened, mainly by forest loss. Protected areas such as Tubbataha Reefs and the Puerto Princesa Underground River help conserve it.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#a16207\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#a16207\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Philippine eagle</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">One of the world’s largest eagles</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#78350f\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#78350f\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Philippine tarsier</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Tiny primate with huge eyes</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#475569\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#475569\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Tamaraw</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Small buffalo found only on Mindoro</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rafflesia</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Giant flowers, several species endemic</text></svg>","c":"Four species found only in the Philippines"}]},"magsaysay":{"t":"Ramon Magsaysay’s life","c":"Ramon Magsaysay was the seventh president of the Philippines, serving from 1953 until his death in 1957. As defence secretary, he led the campaign against the communist Hukbalahap rebellion, combining military action with land and amnesty offers. As president, he was hugely popular for opening the presidential palace to ordinary people and travelling to the provinces. He died when his plane crashed on Mount Manunggal in Cebu. The Ramon Magsaysay Award, often called Asia’s Nobel Prize, is named after him.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1907</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Iba, Zambales</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1950</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Becomes defence secretary</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1953</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Elected president</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Mar 1957</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies in a plane crash in Cebu</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1957</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Ramon Magsaysay Award established</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Magsaysay’s life"}]},"delpilar":{"t":"Marcelo H. del Pilar’s life","c":"Marcelo H. del Pilar was a Filipino lawyer, journalist and leader of the Propaganda Movement, which campaigned peacefully for reforms under Spanish rule. Writing in Tagalog and Spanish, he criticised the power of the friars. He co-founded the newspaper Diariong Tagalog and, after moving to Spain in 1888, became editor of La Solidaridad, the movement’s main newspaper. He died of tuberculosis in Barcelona in 1896, shortly before the revolution began.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1850</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Bulakan, Bulacan</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1882</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Co-founds Diariong Tagalog</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1888</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Leaves for Spain</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1889</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Becomes editor of La Solidaridad</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1896</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies in Barcelona</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in del Pilar’s life"}]},"sora":{"t":"Tandang Sora’s life","c":"Melchora Aquino, known as Tandang Sora, was a Filipino revolutionary heroine called the ‘Mother of the Katipunan’. When the revolution began in 1896, she was already 84 years old, but she fed, sheltered and nursed wounded Katipuneros at her store and home. Arrested by the Spanish, she refused to give information and was exiled to the Mariana Islands. She returned after the Americans took over, and died in 1919 at the age of 107.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1812</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Caloocan</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Aug 1896</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Helps the Katipunan, aged 84</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1896</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Arrested and exiled to the Marianas</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1903</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Returns to the Philippines</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1919</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies, aged 107</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Tandang Sora’s life"}]},"lorenzoruiz":{"t":"San Lorenzo Ruiz’s life","c":"Lorenzo Ruiz was the first Filipino saint. Born in Binondo, Manila, to a Chinese father and a Filipina mother, he was a calligrapher for the Dominican church. In 1636, accused of a crime, he sailed with Dominican missionaries to Japan, where Christianity was banned. They were arrested and tortured, and Ruiz was martyred in Nagasaki in 1637 for refusing to renounce his faith. He was beatified in Manila in 1981, the first beatification held outside the Vatican, and canonised in 1987.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">c.1600</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Binondo, Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1636</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sails to Japan with missionaries</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1637</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Martyred in Nagasaki</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1981</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Beatified in Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1987</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Canonised: the first Filipino saint</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in his life"}]},"fedelmundo":{"t":"Fe del Mundo’s life","c":"Fe del Mundo was a Filipino paediatrician and National Scientist who devoted over 80 years to children’s health. She is often said to have been the first woman admitted to Harvard Medical School’s paediatrics programme, in 1936. In 1957, she founded the first paediatric hospital in the Philippines, now the Fe del Mundo Medical Center. She did research on jaundice, dengue and other childhood diseases and promoted immunisation and family planning in rural areas.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 288\" width=\"640\" height=\"288\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"272\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1911</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1933</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Graduates in medicine, top of her class</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1936</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Studies paediatrics at Harvard</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1957</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Founds the first children’s hospital</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1980</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Named National Scientist</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"244\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2011</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies, aged 99</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in her life"}]},"jluna":{"t":"Juan Luna’s life","c":"Juan Luna was a Filipino painter, one of the first internationally recognised Filipino artists. His huge painting ‘Spoliarium’, showing fallen gladiators being dragged from a Roman arena, won a gold medal at the Madrid Exposition of Fine Arts in 1884, a triumph celebrated by Filipino reformists as proof of their equality with Europeans. It now hangs in the National Museum in Manila. He later supported the revolution and was a diplomat for the Philippine Republic. His brother was General Antonio Luna.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1857</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Badoc, Ilocos Norte</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1884</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Spoliarium wins a gold medal in Madrid</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1890s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Lives and paints in Paris</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1898</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Diplomat for the revolutionary government</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1899</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies in Hong Kong</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Juan Luna’s life"}]},"balagtas":{"t":"Francisco Balagtas’s life","c":"Francisco Balagtas, also known as Francisco Baltazar, was a Filipino poet, considered one of the greatest writers in Tagalog. His masterpiece, ‘Florante at Laura’ (1838), is a long metrical romance set in Albania, widely read as a hidden criticism of Spanish rule. It has been studied in Philippine schools for generations. The Balagtasan, a debate in verse, is named in his honour, and the Philippines celebrates Balagtas Day on 2 April, his birthday.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1788</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Panginay, Bulacan</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1830s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Imprisoned after a rivalry over a woman</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1838</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Florante at Laura is published</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1862</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies in Udyong, Bataan</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1924</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The first Balagtasan is held</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Balagtas’s life"}]},"salonga":{"t":"Lea Salonga’s career","c":"Lea Salonga is a Filipino singer and actress, famous worldwide for her roles in musical theatre. At 18, she won the lead role of Kim in the musical ‘Miss Saigon’ in London, then on Broadway, winning a Tony Award in 1991, the first Asian woman to do so. She provided the singing voice of two Disney princesses, Jasmine in ‘Aladdin’ and Mulan, and was named a Disney Legend in 2011. She has also starred in ‘Les Misérables’ on Broadway.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 288\" width=\"640\" height=\"288\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"272\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1971</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1989</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Stars in Miss Saigon in London</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1991</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Wins a Tony Award on Broadway</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1992</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Jasmine’s singing voice in Aladdin</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1998</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Mulan’s singing voice</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"244\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2011</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Named a Disney Legend</text></svg>","c":"Key moments in her career"}]},"hidilyn":{"t":"Hidilyn Diaz’s Olympic journey","c":"Hidilyn Diaz is a Filipino weightlifter who won the Philippines’ first ever Olympic gold medal, at the Tokyo Olympics in 2021, in the women’s 55-kilogram class, setting an Olympic record. She grew up in Zamboanga City and began lifting with homemade weights of pipes and concrete. She had earlier won silver at the 2016 Rio Olympics, the first Olympic medal for a Filipina. She has competed at four Olympic Games.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1991</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Zamboanga City</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2008</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">First Olympics, aged 17</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2016</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Silver medal in Rio de Janeiro</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2018</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Asian Games gold</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2021</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Olympic gold in Tokyo: a first for the Philippines</text></svg>","c":"From Zamboanga to Olympic gold"}]},"pacquiao":{"t":"Manny Pacquiao’s career","c":"Manny Pacquiao is a Filipino boxer and politician, the only boxer to have won world titles in eight different weight divisions. Born into poverty in Bukidnon, he left home as a teenager and turned professional at 16. Known as ‘Pacman’, he became one of the most famous athletes in Asia. He served as a congressman and a senator, ran for president in 2022, and returned to the ring in 2025.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 288\" width=\"640\" height=\"288\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"272\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1978</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Kibawe, Bukidnon</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1995</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Turns professional, aged 16</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1998</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">First world title</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2010</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Wins his eighth-division world title</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2016–22</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Serves as a senator</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"244\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2025</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Returns to boxing</text></svg>","c":"Key moments in his career"}]},"amorsolo":{"t":"Fernando Amorsolo’s life","c":"Fernando Amorsolo was a Filipino painter best known for sunlit scenes of rural life, rice planting and harvest, and portraits of Filipino women. He perfected a backlighting technique, painting figures glowing against bright sunlight. He also painted portraits, historical scenes and the destruction of Manila in the Second World War. In 1972, he was posthumously named the first National Artist of the Philippines.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1892</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Born in Paco, Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1914</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Graduates from the University of the Philippines art school</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1920s–30s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Famous for sunlit rural scenes</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1940s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Paints wartime Manila</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1972</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dies; named first National Artist</text></svg>","c":"Key dates in Amorsolo’s life"}]},"phlit":{"t":"Landmarks of Philippine literature","c":"Philippine literature is written in many languages, including Filipino, English, Spanish and regional languages such as Cebuano and Ilocano. It began with oral traditions: epics, riddles, proverbs and songs. Spanish rule brought religious texts and metrical romances, and reformist writers in the 1880s used novels to call for change. In the American period, writing in English flourished. National Artists for Literature include Nick Joaquin, F. Sionil José and Bienvenido Lumbera.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Oral epics</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Hudhud of the Ifugao; Darangen of the Maranao</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Florante at Laura, 1838</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Francisco Balagtas’s Tagalog romance</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Noli Me Tángere, 1887</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">José Rizal’s novel of colonial abuse</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Modern writing</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Nick Joaquin, F. Sionil José and others</text></svg>","c":"Four landmarks"}]},"opm":{"t":"Original Pilipino Music through the years","c":"Original Pilipino Music, or OPM, means popular songs written and performed by Filipinos. The term took off in the 1970s with the ‘Manila Sound’ and singer-songwriters, and the Metro Manila Popular Music Festival, which produced hits such as ‘Anak’ by Freddie Aguilar. The 1990s saw a band explosion led by groups such as the Eraserheads. Since the 2010s, streaming has helped new singers and P-pop groups such as SB19 reach fans at home and abroad.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1970s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Manila Sound and singer-songwriters</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1977</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Metro Manila Popular Music Festival begins</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1990s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The band explosion</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2010s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Streaming brings new artists</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2020s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">P-pop groups gain global fans</text></svg>","c":"OPM through the decades"}]},"phdance":{"t":"Some traditional Philippine dances","c":"Philippine music and dance reflect the country’s many cultures: Indigenous peoples of the Cordillera and Mindanao, Muslim communities of the south, and centuries of Spanish and American influence. Many folk dances were documented by Francisca Reyes Aquino from the 1920s. Traditional instruments include the kulintang, a row of gongs, the bamboo angklung and the rondalla string band. The Bayanihan Philippine National Folk Dance Company has performed around the world.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 306\" width=\"620\" height=\"306\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"600\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Tinikling</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dancers step between clapping bamboo poles</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"600\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Singkil</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Maranao royal dance with fans and poles</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"158\" width=\"600\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Pandanggo sa Ilaw</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dancing with oil lamps balanced on head and hands</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"232\" width=\"600\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#db2777\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Cariñosa</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">A flirtatious dance with fan and handkerchief</text></svg>","c":"Four well-known folk dances"}]},"kundiman":{"t":"Facts about the kundiman","c":"The kundiman is a traditional Filipino love song, slow and melancholic, usually in a minor key that shifts to a major key in its second half. Many kundiman are songs of a lover’s devotion, but during the Spanish and American periods, some carried hidden patriotic messages, with the beloved standing for the motherland. Composers such as Francisco Santiago and Nicanor Abelardo turned it into an art song in the early 20th century. Famous examples include ‘Bayan Ko’ and ‘Nasaan Ka Irog’.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#db2777\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#db2777\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">A love song</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Slow, tender and sorrowful</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Minor to major</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Often brightens in the second half</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Hidden meanings</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">The beloved can stand for the country</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Art songs</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Developed by Santiago and Abelardo</text></svg>","c":"Four features of the kundiman"}]},"phcinema":{"t":"Philippine cinema through the years","c":"Filipino films have been made since the early 20th century. The 1950s are remembered as a first golden age of big studios, and the 1970s and early 80s as a second, when directors such as Lino Brocka and Ishmael Bernal made films about poverty and injustice. Digital cameras and festivals such as Cinemalaya, from 2005, boosted independent cinema, and Filipino films and actors have since won awards at Cannes, Berlin and Venice.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 246\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"34\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1919</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dalagang Bukid: an early Filipino-made feature</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1950s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"81\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">First golden age of the big studios</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"118\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1970s–80s</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Second golden age: Brocka and Bernal</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2005</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Cinemalaya festival boosts independent films</text><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"202\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2009</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Brillante Mendoza wins best director at Cannes</text></svg>","c":"Key moments in Philippine film"}]},"zarzuela":{"t":"Facts about the sarswela","c":"The sarswela is a form of musical theatre that mixes spoken dialogue, songs and dance, adapted from the Spanish zarzuela in the late 19th century. Filipino writers and composers made it their own, writing in Tagalog and regional languages about love, family and social issues, and sometimes anti-colonial themes. It was the most popular entertainment in the early 1900s, until films took over. ‘Walang Sugat’ (1902) by Severino Reyes is one of the best-known works.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 610 158\" width=\"610\" height=\"158\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Spanish roots</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">From the zarzuela of Spain</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"10\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Songs and speech</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Dialogue, music and dance together</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Local languages</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Written in Tagalog and regional languages</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"84\" width=\"290\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ca8a04\" fill-opacity=\".2\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Walang Sugat, 1902</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">A famous sarswela by Severino Reyes</text></svg>","c":"Four features of the sarswela"}]},"phpower":{"t":"Where Philippine electricity comes from","c":"The Philippine power industry generates, transmits and distributes electricity across more than 7,600 islands, which makes building a single national grid difficult. Since 2001, generation has been run largely by private companies. Coal produces most of the electricity, followed by renewables and natural gas. The Philippines is one of the world’s leading producers of geothermal power, and solar and offshore wind are growing quickly. Electricity prices are among the highest in Southeast Asia. Shares are approximate for the early 2020s.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 184\" width=\"620\" height=\"184\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:620px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><text x=\"130\" y=\"31\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Coal</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"12\" width=\"330.0\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#475569\"/><text x=\"478\" y=\"31\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">about 60%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Renewables</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"52\" width=\"121.0\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"269\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">about 22% (geothermal, hydro, solar, wind)</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Natural gas</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"92\" width=\"82.5\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#0891b2\"/><text x=\"230.5\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">about 15%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Oil</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"132\" width=\"11.0\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#a16207\"/><text x=\"159\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">about 2%</text></svg>","c":"Approximate share of electricity generated, early 2020s"}]},"japancountry":{"t":"The flag of Japan","c":"Japan’s flag is known as the Hinomaru, ‘circle of the sun’, reflecting the country’s name, Nihon, which means ‘origin of the sun’. A red disc on a white field, it has been used for centuries and was made official by law in 1999. Its simplicity has made it one of the world’s most recognisable flags.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/jp.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#d62828\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red disc: the sun</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: honesty and purity (popular</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"137\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">meaning)</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"chinacountry":{"t":"The flag of China","c":"China’s flag, adopted in 1949 when the People’s Republic was founded, is called the Five-starred Red Flag. Red stands for the communist revolution. The large star represents the Communist Party, and the four smaller stars, which point towards it, the unity of the people around the party.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/cn.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#d62828\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: the communist revolution</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#f6c90e\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Large star: the Communist Party</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#f6c90e\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Four small stars: the people united</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"indiacountry":{"t":"The flag of India","c":"India’s flag, the Tiranga (‘tricolour’), was adopted on 22 July 1947, shortly before independence. In the centre is the Ashoka Chakra, a navy-blue wheel with 24 spokes taken from the lion capital of Emperor Ashoka, representing the wheel of law and of progress. By law, the flag is meant to be made of khadi, hand-spun cloth.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/in.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ff9933\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Saffron: courage and sacrifice</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: peace and truth</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#138808\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: faith, growth and fertility</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#000080\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Wheel: law and progress (24 spokes)</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"indonesiacountry":{"t":"The flag of Indonesia","c":"Indonesia’s flag, called Sang Saka Merah Putih (the ‘sacred red and white’), was first raised when independence was declared on 17 August 1945. Its colours go back to the Majapahit Empire. It is almost identical to the flag of Monaco, differing only in its proportions.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/id.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#d62828\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: courage</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: purity</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"pakistancountry":{"t":"The flag of Pakistan","c":"Pakistan’s flag was adopted just before independence in August 1947. The dark green field stands for the country’s Muslim majority and the white stripe for its religious minorities. The crescent represents progress and the star light and knowledge.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/pk.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#01411c\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: the Muslim majority</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: religious minorities</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crescent: progress</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Star: light and knowledge</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"vietnamcountry":{"t":"The flag of Vietnam","c":"Vietnam’s flag, a yellow star on a red field, was first used by the Viet Minh independence movement in 1940 and became the flag of the whole country after reunification in 1976. The five points of the star are said to represent workers, farmers, intellectuals, young people and soldiers.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/vn.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#da251d\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: revolution and sacrifice</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffcd00\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Star’s five points: the five</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"137\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">groups of society</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"southkoreacountry":{"t":"The flag of South Korea","c":"South Korea’s flag, the Taegukgi, has a red and blue taegeuk at its centre, representing the balance of opposites, yin and yang. Around it are four black trigrams from the I Ching, standing for heaven, earth, water and fire. It was first used in the 1880s.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/kr.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: peace and purity</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#cd2e3a\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red and blue taegeuk: balance of</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"117\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">opposites</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Four trigrams: heaven, earth,</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"157\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">water, fire</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"irancountry":{"t":"The flag of Iran","c":"Iran’s current flag was adopted in 1980, after the Islamic Revolution. The red emblem in the centre is a stylised form of the word ‘Allah’. Along the edges of the green and red stripes, the phrase ‘Allahu akbar’ (‘God is great’) is written 22 times in Kufic script, marking the date of the revolution, 22 Bahman in the Iranian calendar.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/ir.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#239f40\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: Islam and growth</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: peace</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#da0000\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: courage and martyrdom</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#da0000\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Emblem: a stylised ‘Allah’</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"turkeycountry":{"t":"The flag of Türkiye","c":"Türkiye’s flag, called Ay Yıldız (‘moon star’), shows a white crescent and star on red. Its design comes from the late Ottoman Empire, and its exact proportions were fixed by law in 1936. Popular legends link the image to the reflection of the moon and a star in pools of soldiers’ blood after a battle.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/tr.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e30a17\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: often linked to the blood of</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">martyrs</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crescent and star: long-used</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"137\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">symbols of the land</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"saudicountry":{"t":"The flag of Saudi Arabia","c":"Saudi Arabia’s flag carries the Shahada, the Islamic declaration of faith: ‘There is no god but God; Muhammad is the Messenger of God’, above a sword. Because it contains a holy text, it is never flown at half-mast, and it is made so that the writing reads correctly from both sides.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/sa.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#006c35\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: Islam</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Writing: the Shahada, declaration</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"117\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">of faith</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sword: justice and strength</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"thailandcountry":{"t":"The flag of Thailand","c":"Thailand’s flag, the Trairanga (‘tricolour’), was adopted in 1917 by King Vajiravudh. Its five horizontal stripes of red, white and blue, with a wide blue band in the middle, represent the nation, religion and monarchy, the three pillars of Thai identity.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/th.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#a51931\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: the nation (land and people)</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: religion</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2d2a4a\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blue: the monarchy</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"malaysiacountry":{"t":"The flag of Malaysia","c":"Malaysia’s flag is called the Jalur Gemilang, ‘stripes of glory’. Its 14 red and white stripes and the 14-pointed star stand for the equal status of the 13 states and the federal government. The crescent represents Islam, the official religion, and yellow is the royal colour of the Malay rulers.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/my.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#cc0001\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">14 stripes: the 13 states and</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">federal government</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#010066\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blue: unity of the people</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffcc00\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crescent: Islam</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffcc00\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">14-pointed star: unity; yellow is</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"177\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">royal</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"singaporecountry":{"t":"The flag of Singapore","c":"Singapore’s flag was adopted in 1959, when it became self-governing, and kept at independence in 1965. The crescent moon represents a young nation on the rise, and its five stars stand for the nation’s ideals: democracy, peace, progress, justice and equality.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/sg.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ef3340\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: universal brotherhood and</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">equality</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: purity and virtue</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crescent: a young nation on the rise</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Five stars: five national ideals</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"myanmarcountry":{"t":"The flag of Myanmar","c":"Myanmar’s current flag was introduced in 2010, along with a new constitution. Its three horizontal stripes of yellow, green and red carry a large white five-pointed star in the centre, representing the union of the country.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/mm.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fecb00\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Yellow: solidarity</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#34b233\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: peace and the green land</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ea2839\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: courage and determination</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White star: the union</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"cambodiacountry":{"t":"The flag of Cambodia","c":"Cambodia’s flag shows the temple of Angkor Wat in white on a red band between two blue stripes, making it one of very few national flags to feature a building. Versions of the flag with Angkor Wat have been used since the 1850s, and the current flag was restored in 1993 along with the monarchy.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/kh.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#032ea1\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blue: the monarchy</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e00025\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: the nation</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Angkor Wat: religion and heritage</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"laoscountry":{"t":"The flag of Laos","c":"The flag of Laos was first used by the Lao independence movement in the 1940s and became the national flag in 1975. The white disc is said to represent the full moon over the Mekong River, and also the unity of the people under the government.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/la.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ce1126\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: the blood shed for freedom</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#002868\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blue: the Mekong and the nation’s</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"117\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">wealth</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White disc: the full moon, and unity</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"bruneicountry":{"t":"The flag of Brunei","c":"Brunei’s flag has a yellow field, the colour of the sultan, crossed by diagonal white and black stripes representing his chief ministers. In the centre is the national crest in red, with an umbrella, wings, hands and a crescent, inscribed with the national motto in Arabic script: ‘Always in service with God’s guidance’.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/bn.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#f7e017\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Yellow: the sultan</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White and black stripes: chief</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"117\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">ministers</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#cf1126\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Crest: the state and Islam</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"timorlestecountry":{"t":"The flag of Timor-Leste","c":"Timor-Leste’s flag was first raised in 1975 and again at the restoration of independence on 20 May 2002. Its colours tell the story of the country’s struggle: a black triangle over a yellow arrowhead on a red field, with a white star as a guiding light.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/tl.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#dc241f\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: the struggle for liberation</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffc726\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Yellow: traces of colonialism</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Black: hardships to be overcome</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White star: hope and peace</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"bangladeshcountry":{"t":"The flag of Bangladesh","c":"Bangladesh’s flag, adopted in 1972, shows a red disc on a dark green field. The disc is set slightly towards the hoist, so it appears centred when the flag flies. The red represents the sun rising over Bengal and the blood of those who died in the 1971 Liberation War.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/bd.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#006a4e\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: the land and its vitality</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#f42a41\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red disc: the rising sun and the</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"137\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">sacrifice of 1971</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"israelcountry":{"t":"The flag of Israel","c":"Israel’s flag, adopted in 1948, shows a blue Star of David, an ancient Jewish symbol, between two blue stripes on white. The design is based on the tallit, the Jewish prayer shawl, which is white with blue or black stripes.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/il.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"52\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#0038b8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blue stripes: a Jewish prayer shawl</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"92\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#0038b8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Star of David: a Jewish symbol</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"132\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White background</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"uaecountry":{"t":"The flag of the United Arab Emirates","c":"The flag of the United Arab Emirates was adopted on 2 December 1971, when the federation was formed. Its red, green, white and black are the Pan-Arab colours, used in the flags of many Arab countries and linked to the Arab Revolt against Ottoman rule in 1916.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/ae.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ef3340\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: the Pan-Arab colours</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#00843d\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Black</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"iraqcountry":{"t":"The flag of Iraq","c":"Iraq’s flag uses the Pan-Arab colours red, white and black. Since 2008, the green words in the centre have been the takbir, ‘Allahu akbar’ (‘God is great’), written in Kufic script. The three green stars of earlier versions were removed at that time.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/iq.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ce1126\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: courage</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: generosity</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Black: past hardship</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#007a3d\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green writing: ‘God is great’</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"jordancountry":{"t":"The flag of Jordan","c":"Jordan’s flag is based on the flag of the Arab Revolt of 1916. Its three stripes stand for three historic Arab caliphates, and the red triangle for the ruling Hashemite family. The white seven-pointed star represents the seven verses of the opening chapter of the Qur’an, and the unity of Arab peoples.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 224\" width=\"620\" height=\"224\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/jo.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"22\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"22\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"18\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"36\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Black: the Abbasid Caliphate</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"58\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: the Umayyad Caliphate</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"98\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#007a3d\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: the Fatimid Caliphate</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"138\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ce1126\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red triangle: the Hashemite dynasty</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"178\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Seven-pointed star: the Qur’an’s</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"203\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">first chapter</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"nigeriacountry":{"t":"The flag of Nigeria","c":"Nigeria’s flag was designed in 1959 by Michael Taiwo Akinkunmi, a student, who won a national competition. It was first raised at independence on 1 October 1960. Its three vertical bands are green, white and green.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/ng.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#008751\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: forests and natural wealth</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: peace and unity</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"egyptcountry":{"t":"The flag of Egypt","c":"Egypt’s flag has red, white and black horizontal stripes, the colours of the Arab Liberation flag used after the 1952 revolution. In the centre is the Eagle of Saladin in gold, holding a scroll with the country’s name in Arabic.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/eg.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ce1126\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: struggle and sacrifice</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">White: the peaceful 1952 revolution</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Black: the end of oppression</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#c09300\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Eagle of Saladin: the national</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"177\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">emblem</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"southafricacountry":{"t":"The flag of South Africa","c":"South Africa’s flag was adopted in 1994, when apartheid ended and the country held its first democratic elections. Its six colours have no official meanings, but the Y shape is widely seen as the coming together of the country’s different peoples, taking the road ahead in unity.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/za.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#007a4d\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Y shape: diverse peoples coming</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">together</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#111111\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Black, green and gold</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#de3831\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red, white and blue</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffb612\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">No official meanings for the colours</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]},"ethiopiacountry":{"t":"The flag of Ethiopia","c":"Ethiopia’s green, yellow and red were adopted in the 1890s, and because Ethiopia was never colonised, they inspired many other African flags, becoming the Pan-African colours. The blue disc with a yellow star was added in 1996.","items":[{"w":1,"s":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 212\" width=\"620\" height=\"212\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" style=\"width:600px;max-width:100%;height:auto\"><image href=\"flags/et.svg\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"32\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#078930\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Green: the land and hope</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"72\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fcdd09\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Yellow: peace and harmony</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"112\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#da121a\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Red: strength and sacrifice</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#0f47af\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\".4\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Blue disc and star: unity and</text><text x=\"312\" y=\"177\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">equality</text></svg>","c":"The flag and what its parts stand for"}]}});
